816411</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat.1000140-Blom1"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Blom</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Rytkonen</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Vasquez</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Lindahl</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Dahlback</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>A novel interaction between type IV pili of <italic>Neisseria gonorrhoeae</italic> and the human complement regulator C4B-binding protein.</article-title><source>J Immunol</source><volume>166</volume><fpage>6764</fpage><lpage>6770</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11359834</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat.1000140-Berggard1"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Berggard</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Johnsson</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Mooi</surname><given-names>FR</given-names></name><name><surname>Lindahl</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title><italic>Bordetella pertussis</italic> binds the human complement regulator C4BP: role of filamentous hemagglutinin.</article-title><source>Infect Immun</source><volume>65</volume><fpage>3638</fpage><lpage>3643</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9284130</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat.1000140-Hellwage1"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hellwage</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Meri</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Heikkila</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Alitalo</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Panelius</surname><given-names>J</g